### Description

Hi, sometimes the most accurate option may not be retrieved in completion suggester.
```json
PUT /test
{
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "suggest": {
        "type": "completion",
        "analyzer": "standard",
        "preserve_separators": false,
        "preserve_position_increments": false,
        "max_input_length": 30
      }
    }
  }
}

POST _bulk
{"index": {"_index": "test", "_id": "1"}}
{"suggest":{"input":["ab"]}}
{"index": {"_index": "test", "_id": "2"}}
{"suggest":{"input":["a bc"]}}
{"index": {"_index": "test", "_id": "3"}}
{"suggest":{"input":["a bc1"]}}
{"index": {"_index": "test", "_id": "4"}}
{"suggest":{"input":["a b"]}}

GET /test/_search
{
	"suggest": {
		"suggest": {
			"completion": {
				"field": "suggest",
				"size": 100
			},
			"prefix": "ab"
		}
	}
}
```
The order in which the results were retrieved was:
```text
a b
a bc
a bc1
ab
```
When the weight is the same, the return result of completion is in lexicographical order. Considering [ "preserve_separators" : false ], expected result was:
```
ab
a b
a bc
a bc123
```
or
```
a b
ab
a bc
a bc123
```
If there are 1000+ documents in the index with formats such as "a bxxx" or "a b xxx", then the most matching terms (ab) will not be retrieved, even if the lexicographical order of the characters after removing the separators is higher.

