### Elasticsearch Version

9.4.5

### Installed Plugins

_No response_

### Java Version

_bundled_

### OS Version

*

### Problem Description

In `ScaledFloatFieldMapper.parseCreateField`, the ignore_malformed catch block has two branches:

```
context.addIgnoredField(mappedFieldType.name());   // always: just Set.add, never touches the parser
if (isSourceSynthetic) {
    FallbackPostMapper.capture(context, fullPath(), FallbackPostMapper.Reason.MALFORMED); // consumes the value's tokens
}
return;
```

Only the synthetic-source branch calls `FallbackPostMapper.capture`, which (via `XContentDataHelper.encodeToken`) copies — and thereby consumes — the full current token structure. So when the malformed value is a multi-token structure (a JSON object/array, the synthetic-source path happens to leave the parser correctly positioned as a side effect of capturing the value, while the stored-source path returns with the object's `START_OBJECT…END_OBJECT` still unconsumed, desyncing the parser from the document tree for everything parsed afterward. 



### Steps to Reproduce

```
PUT /repro-synthetic
{ "settings": { "index.mapping.source.mode": "synthetic" },
  "mappings": { "properties": {
    "usage": { "type": "scaled_float", "scaling_factor": 100, "ignore_malformed": true },
    "trailing": { "type": "keyword" }
  }}}

PUT /repro-stored
{ "settings": { "index.mapping.source.mode": "stored" },
  "mappings": { "properties": {
    "usage": { "type": "scaled_float", "scaling_factor": 100, "ignore_malformed": true },
    "trailing": { "type": "keyword" }
  }}}

PUT /repro-synthetic/_doc/1
{ "usage": { "output_tokens": "237", "input_tokens": "2995" }, "trailing": "should-be-searchable" }

PUT /repro-stored/_doc/1
{ "usage": { "output_tokens": "237", "input_tokens": "2995" }, "trailing": "should-be-searchable" }
```

The stored branch fails, because malformed data is not processed correctly. 

