### Describe the Bug

```python
from typing import Literal

class A:
    a_attr: int

    @property
    def is_a(self) -> bool: raise NotImplementedError()

class B:
    @property
    def is_a(self) -> Literal[False]: raise NotImplementedError()

def foo(x: A | B) -> None:
    print(x.a_attr)
    assert x.is_a
    print(x.a_attr)
```

Python: 3.12

In the above example, mypy uses the `assert` in `foo` to narrow the type of `x` to `A`. I recognizes that the assert will fail if `x` is an instance of `B` because `B.is_a` returns `False`. So only the first access to `x.a_attr` is flagged. See [this mypy Playground](https://mypy-play.net/?gist=962f319756e3178c9333d5fec1808c9b).

Pyrefly does not do the same and flags both accesses to `x.a_attr`.

