### Describe the Bug

unfortunately this is a pretty convoluted example. this is as minimal as i could get it:

```py
from collections.abc import Callable
from typing import Concatenate, overload, assert_type


class ClassAndInstanceMethod[T, **ClsParams, ClsResult, **SelfParams, SelfResult]:
    @overload
    def __get__(
        self, instance: T, owner: type[T]
    ) -> Callable[SelfParams, SelfResult]: ...
    @overload
    def __get__(
        self, instance: None, owner: type[T]
    ) -> Callable[ClsParams, ClsResult]: ...

    def __get__(
        self, instance: T | None, owner: type[T]
    ) -> Callable[ClsParams, ClsResult] | Callable[SelfParams, SelfResult]: ...


class A[T, **P, ClsResult, InstanceResult](
    ClassAndInstanceMethod[T, P, ClsResult, P, InstanceResult]
):
    def __init__(
        self, class_method: Callable[Concatenate[type[T], P], ClsResult]
    ) -> None: ...


class B[T, **P, R](A[T, P, type[R], R]): ...


class Foo:
    @B
    @classmethod
    def fn(cls) -> type[str]: ...


assert_type(Foo().fn(), str) # error, type is `Unknown`
assert_type(Foo.fn(), type[str]) # error, type is `type[Any]`
```

the use case is a decorator that allows a method to have a different signature depending on whether it's called on the instance or the class.

these type assertions pass in both [pyright](https://basedpyright.com/?pythonVersion=3.15&typeCheckingMode=all&reportUnusedParameter=false&%2BCcImckV0rncHkxnicstVPpkEr8WlsgXgrAtoeNJtMEecURU0WQMRsthEoAAfKC4g5KMD7Q7cEmnc5U%2B4MWkvBkfWoOHJ5P7NaU0p4vN6M-U-I1swHAthWGx2KBOSIlRLMw1NYpQDxrTFIVn-RELeJ2FzuMW%2BALBULuqCeg3BpRJ-3rXzB8kXdoUzo8iYCdDw0PIzqopTOgzGCCBELaLZa830yTyOQyMLHU6p5perPqm73OWbe2cx3jqv2ABCCdiSeyzRmbp2Sa7C6UC5zo6s7EnUAAYmAwLmFt0pyDJ7W45C81AecAsDMbDgNSrzGE1iAARyd2xjFAAF4oDsIxTBJGZDzAGYLjwB9oKUT8LnYf8gJAmgwPMCCj1gx8LiULtP2aJC2CAA) and [ty](https://play.ty.dev/60458263-4f8a-4fe7-b8d6-2249053e4b7b)

